Description: Part of the surveyverse, a tidy and reproducible framework for
    survey analysis, surveywts provides the full weight adjustment workflow.
    Working with survey objects from the surveyverse ecosystem, analysts can
    handle unit nonresponse through weighting-class or propensity-based
    adjustment, calibrate to census or survey-based benchmarks using raking,
    GREG, logit-bounded, or post-stratification estimators, and generate
    variance estimation weights via bootstrap, jackknife, BRR, and related
    replicate-weight schemes. For non-probability samples, implements inverse
    probability weighting via logistic regression with an optional calibration
    GEE that guarantees exact covariate balance. Diagnostic functions report
    effective sample size, weight variability, and full distributional
    profiles, and every adjustment is recorded in a structured history
    attached to the result object.
